  "published": "2026-11-05T07:46:49Z",
  "modified": "2026-11-05T07:46:49Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the MSL decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116146.patch: destroy the whole image list\n       instead of only its first frame in MSLPopImage(), MSLStartElement(),\n       MSLEndElement() and ProcessMSLScript() in coders/msl.c\n     - CVE-2026-116146\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: NULL pointer dereference in the DJVU decoder\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116147.patch: stop reading pages when\n       CloneImageList() fails in ReadDJVUImage() in coders/djvu.c\n     - CVE-2026-116147\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: stack buffer over-write when reading bzip2-compressed\n     data\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116149.patch: mark the blob as failed on a\n       bzip2 read error and do not call BZ2_bzread() again on a failed blob\n       in ReadBlob() in magick/blob.c\n     - CVE-2026-116149\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak when parsing XMP profiles\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116155.patch: free the parameter entity\n       values in ParseInternalDoctype() in magick/xml-tree.c\n     - CVE-2026-116155\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leaks in PerlMagick\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116157.patch: free the string returned by\n       InterpretImageProperties() in SetAttribute(), Mogrify() and Montage()\n       in PerlMagick/quantum/quantum.xs.in\n     - CVE-2026-116157\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: memory leak in the -cdl option\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-116159.patch: destroy the color correction\n       collection string in MogrifyImage() in wand/mogrify.c\n     - CVE-2026-116159",
